; A `break &b` carrying a reference into a repeat-body frame-local out of the
; loop, then returned, must be rejected — the pointee dies with the frame. The
; break-value promotion (which moves heap CONSTRUCTIONS to the caller page)
; must NOT silently accept a bare frame-local REFERENCE: `&b`'s operator head is
; not collected, so b is never promoted/marked, and the return-site escape
; check fires as it does for a direct `return &b`.
function bad() returns pointer[int]
{
    let p repeat
    {
        var b 5
        break &b
    }
    return p
}
